{"title":"Team selection test","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>team selection test</b> (TST), or <b>team selection exam</b> (TSE) is a test given to top finishers in a national olympiad to determine the nation's team for an international olympiad such as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BMO\" title=\"BMO\">BMO</a>.\n</p><p>Many individuals use TSTs as practice olympiads.   Those from China, Romania, and the USA are particularly popular.  China's, in particular, is notoriously difficult.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Team_selection_test&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php\">AoPS/Mathlinks Resources page, containing links to the TSTs of many countries</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.unl.edu/amc/a-activities/a7-problems/problemarchive.html\">AMC page containing USA TSTs to the year 2003</a></li></ul>\n<p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Team_selection_test&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Hello&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Hello (page does not exist)\">Template:Hello</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018111619\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 12/1